Aerie-Purpose: Move the address pill, Back, Forward, Reload and the rest of the toolbar into the Aerie sidebar, take the toolbar row away from the top of the window, and make the sidebar's top row the window's drag handle.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/views/frame (browser_view.cc, vertical_tab_strip_region_view.*, layout/browser_view_tabbed_layout_impl.cc, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/ui/views/toolbar (toolbar_view.cc, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #215 (items 1 and 2 of the rest of #177). All the work is in the overlay, chrome/browser/ui/views/aerie_sidebar
(AerieSidebarView::AdoptToolbar, AerieSidebarTopRow, aerie_sidebar_toolbar_hook.h); these hooks only call it.

- browser_view.cc: right after the toolbar made its buttons (ToolbarView::Init, in AddedToWidget), one call,
  aerie_sidebar::AdoptToolbar, hands the toolbar's views to the sidebar when the layout is the sidebar: the real LocationBarView
  (the address pill), Back, Forward and Reload (found by view id), and the toolbar itself, which keeps the extensions, profile and
  menu buttons and goes to the sidebar's bottom bar. The call also decides about the window controls (where the frame draws them on
  the trailing side, Linux with the custom frame, the sidebar draws its own and the frame's become invisible; a leading exclusion,
  the macOS traffic lights, becomes an inset of the top row). That logic is in the overlay, not in this patch.
- vertical_tab_strip_region_view.*: AdoptAerieToolbar forwards to the sidebar view; the empty part of the top row counts as the window
  caption in IsPositionInWindowCaption (the same hook Helium's top container uses). The sidebar answers before Helium's
  hidden bottom container, which would otherwise claim the whole column.
- browser_view_tabbed_layout_impl.cc: the toolbar is no longer a child of the top container, which the layout already
  handles (IsParentedTo), so the toolbar row is gone. The one change is the top of the collapsed column, which used to
  start under the toolbar and now starts at 0.
- toolbar_view.cc: the toolbar's own "collapse tabs" button stays hidden in the sidebar layout, because the top row has
  the toggle.
- frame/BUILD.gn: the browser_view target depends on the sidebar target, for the hook header.

